## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

In the PR, I propose to convert time zone string to `TimeZone` by converting it to `ZoneId` which uses `ZoneOffset` internally. The `ZoneOffset` class of JDK 8 has a cache already: <a href="http://hg.openjdk.java.net/jdk8/jdk8/jdk/file/687fd7c7986d/src/share/classes/java/time/ZoneOffset.java#l205" rel="nofollow">http://hg.openjdk.java.net/jdk8/jdk8/jdk/file/687fd7c7986d/src/share/classes/java/time/ZoneOffset.java#l205</a> . In this way, there is no need to support cache of time zones in Spark.

The PR removes `computedTimeZones` from `DateTimeUtils`, and uses `ZoneId.of` to convert time zone id string to `ZoneId` and to `TimeZone` at the end.

