… WeekOfYear

## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

The expressions `DayWeek`, `DayOfWeek`, `WeekDay` and `WeekOfYear` are changed to use Proleptic Gregorian calendar instead of the hybrid one (Julian+Gregorian). This was achieved by using Java 8 API for date/timestamp manipulation, in particular the `LocalDate` class.

Week of year calculation is performed according to ISO-8601. The first week of a week-based-year is the first Monday-based week of the standard ISO year that has at least 4 days in the new year (see <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/time/temporal/IsoFields.html" rel="nofollow">https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/time/temporal/IsoFields.html</a>).

## How was this patch tested?

The changes were tested by `DateExpressionsSuite` and `DateFunctionsSuite`.

