## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

Currently OrcColumnarBatchReader returns all the partition column values in the batch read.
In data source V2, we can improve it by returning the required partition column values only.

This PR is part of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="394092086" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/23383" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/23383/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/23383">#23383</a> . As cloud-fan suggested, create a new PR to make review easier.

Also, this PR doesn't improve `OrcFileFormat`, since in the method `buildReaderWithPartitionValues`, the `requiredSchema` filter out all the partition columns, so we can't know which partition column is required.

