<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #22626.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="366704937" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/22626" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/22626/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/22626">#22626</a> from MaxGekk/to_csv.

Lead-authored-by: Maxim Gekk &lt;max.gekk@gmail.com&gt;
Co-authored-by: Maxim Gekk &lt;maxim.gekk@databricks.com&gt;
Signed-off-by: hyukjinkwon &lt;gurwls223@apache.org&gt;

## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

Added new benchmark which forcibly invokes Jackson parser to check overhead of its creation for short and wide JSON strings. Existing benchmarks do not allow to check that due to an optimisation introduced by <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="345461054" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/21909" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/21909/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/21909">#21909</a> for empty schema pushed down to JSON datasource. The `count()` action passes empty schema as required schema to the datasource, and Jackson parser is not created at all in that case.

Besides of new benchmark I also refactored existing benchmarks:
- Added `numIters` to control number of iteration in each benchmark
- Renamed `JSON per-line parsing` -&gt; `count a short column`, `JSON parsing of wide lines` -&gt; `count a wide column`, and `Count a dataset with 10 columns` -&gt; `Select a subset of 10 columns`.

