This PR excludes an existing UT [`writeToOutputStreamUnderflow()`](<a href="https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/master/common/unsafe/src/test/java/org/apache/spark/unsafe/types/UTF8StringSuite.java#L519-L532">https://github.com/apache/spark/blob/master/common/unsafe/src/test/java/org/apache/spark/unsafe/types/UTF8StringSuite.java#L519-L532</a>) in `UTF8StringSuite`.

As discussed [here](<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="257470094" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/19222" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/19222/hovercard?comment_id=177692142&amp;comment_type=review_comment" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/19222#discussion_r177692142">#19222 (comment)</a>), the behavior of this test looks surprising. This test seems to access metadata area of the JVM object where is reserved by `Platform.BYTE_ARRAY_OFFSET`.

This test is introduced thru <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="192704344" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/16089" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/16089/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/16089">#16089</a> by NathanHowell. More specifically, [the commit](<a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/commit/27c102deb1701fe62f776fe4da61dac959270b73/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/commit/27c102deb1701fe62f776fe4da61dac959270b73"><tt>27c102d</tt></a>) `Improve test coverage of UTFString.write` introduced this UT. However, I cannot find any discussion about this UT.

I think that it would be good to exclude this UT.

```java
  public void writeToOutputStreamUnderflow() throws IOException {
    // offset underflow is apparently supported?
    final ByteArrayOutputStream outputStream = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
    final byte[] test = "01234567".getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8);

    for (int i = 1; i &lt;= Platform.BYTE_ARRAY_OFFSET; ++i) {
      new UTF8String(
        new ByteArrayMemoryBlock(test, Platform.BYTE_ARRAY_OFFSET - i, test.length + i))
          .writeTo(outputStream);
      final ByteBuffer buffer = ByteBuffer.wrap(outputStream.toByteArray(), i, test.length);
      assertEquals("01234567", StandardCharsets.UTF_8.decode(buffer).toString());
      outputStream.reset();
    }
  }
```

## How was this patch tested?

Existing UTs

