## How was this patch tested?

Added new test suites in `DataFrameSuites`

Author: Kazuaki Ishizaki &lt;ishizaki@jp.ibm.com&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #17302.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="214347136" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/17302" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/17302/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/17302">#17302</a> from kiszk/SPARK-19959.

…ss in fields

## What changes were proposed in this pull request?
The current master throws `StackOverflowError` in `createDataFrame`/`createDataset` if bean has one's own class in fields;
```
public class SelfClassInFieldBean implements Serializable {
  private SelfClassInFieldBean child;
  ...
}
```
This pr added code to throw `UnsupportedOperationException` in that case as soon as possible.

## How was this patch tested?
Added tests in `JavaDataFrameSuite` and `JavaDatasetSuite`.

Author: Takeshi Yamamuro &lt;yamamuro@apache.org&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #17188.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="212365477" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/17188" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/17188/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/17188">#17188</a> from maropu/SPARK-19751.

## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

This PR introduces the following changes:
1. Move `SparkHadoopWriter` to `core/internal/io/`, so that it's in the same directory with `SparkHadoopMapReduceWriter`;
2. Move `SparkHadoopWriterUtils` to a separated file.

After this PR is merged, we may consolidate `SparkHadoopWriter` and `SparkHadoopMapReduceWriter`, and make the new commit protocol support the old `mapred` package's committer;

## How was this patch tested?

Tested by existing test cases.

