When Spark emits SQL for a string literal, it should wrap the string in single quotes, not double quotes. Databases which adhere more strictly to the ANSI SQL standards, such as Postgres, allow only single-quotes to be used for denoting string literals (see <a href="http://stackoverflow.com/a/1992331/590203" rel="nofollow">http://stackoverflow.com/a/1992331/590203</a>).

