Author: Kazuaki Ishizaki &lt;ishizaki@jp.ibm.com&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #11636.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="139986883" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/11636" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/11636/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/11636">#11636</a> from kiszk/SPARK-13805.

## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

[Spark Coding Style Guide](<a href="https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/SPARK/Spark+Code+Style+Guide" rel="nofollow">https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/SPARK/Spark+Code+Style+Guide</a>) has 100-character limit on lines, but it's disabled for Java since 11/09/15. This PR enables **LineLength** checkstyle again. To help that, this also introduces **RedundantImport** and **RedundantModifier**, too. The following is the diff on `checkstyle.xml`.

```xml
-        &lt;!-- TODO: 11/09/15 disabled - the lengths are currently &gt; 100 in many places --&gt;
-        &lt;!--
         &lt;module name="LineLength"&gt;
             &lt;property name="max" value="100"/&gt;
             &lt;property name="ignorePattern" value="^package.*|^import.*|a href|href|http://|https://|ftp://"/&gt;
         &lt;/module&gt;
-        --&gt;
         &lt;module name="NoLineWrap"/&gt;
         &lt;module name="EmptyBlock"&gt;
             &lt;property name="option" value="TEXT"/&gt;
 -167,5 +164,7
         &lt;/module&gt;
         &lt;module name="CommentsIndentation"/&gt;
         &lt;module name="UnusedImports"/&gt;
+        &lt;module name="RedundantImport"/&gt;
+        &lt;module name="RedundantModifier"/&gt;
```

## How was this patch tested?

Currently, `lint-java` is disabled in Jenkins. It needs a manual test.
After passing the Jenkins tests, `dev/lint-java` should passes locally.

