Author: Cheng Lian &lt;lian@databricks.com&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #10985.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="129860731" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/10985" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/10985/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/10985">#10985</a> from liancheng/sketch-polishing.

Our current Intersect physical operator simply delegates to RDD.intersect. We should remove the Intersect physical operator and simply transform a logical intersect into a semi-join with distinct. This way, we can take advantage of all the benefits of join implementations (e.g. managed memory, code generation, broadcast joins).

After a search, I found one of the mainstream RDBMS did the same. In their query explain, Intersect is replaced by Left-semi Join. Left-semi Join could help outer-join elimination in Optimizer, as shown in the PR: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="124688213" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/10566" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/10566/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/10566">#10566</a>

