Author: Yanbo Liang &lt;ybliang8@gmail.com&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #10378.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="122939022" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/10378" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/10378/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/10378">#10378</a> from yanboliang/leftsemi.

In discussion (SPARK-9552), we proposed a force kill in `killExecutors`. But if there is nothing to kill, it will return back with true (acknowledgement). And then, it causes the certain executor(s) (which is not eligible to kill) adding to pendingToRemove list for further actions.

In this patch, we'd like to change the return semantics. If there is nothing to kill, we will return "false". and therefore  all those non-eligible executors won't be added to the pendingToRemove list.

