Author: Marc Prud'hommeaux &lt;mwp1@cornell.edu&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #9312.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="113703300" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/9312" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/9312/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/9312">#9312</a> from mprudhom/patch-1.

This patch re-enables tests for the Docker JDBC data source. These tests were reverted in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="59614458" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/4872" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/4872/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/4872">#4872</a> due to transitive dependency conflicts introduced by the `docker-client` library. This patch should avoid those problems by using a version of `docker-client` which shades its transitive dependencies and by performing some build-magic to work around problems with that shaded JAR.

In addition, I significantly refactored the tests to simplify the setup and teardown code and to fix several Docker networking issues which caused problems when running in `boot2docker`.

