Author: Reynold Xin &lt;rxin@databricks.com&gt;

<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #8761.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="106501810" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/8761" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/8761/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/8761">#8761</a> from rxin/SPARK-10612.

*Note: this is for master branch only.* The fix for branch-1.5 is at <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="106066196" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/8721" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/8721/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/8721">#8721</a>.

The query execution ID is currently passed from a thread to its children, which is not the intended behavior. This led to `IllegalArgumentException: spark.sql.execution.id is already set` when running queries in parallel, e.g.:
```
(1 to 100).par.foreach { _ =&gt;
  sc.parallelize(1 to 5).map { i =&gt; (i, i) }.toDF("a", "b").count()
}
```
The cause is `SparkContext`'s local properties are inherited by default. This patch adds a way to exclude keys we don't want to be inherited, and makes SQL go through that code path.

