<span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This commit closes pull request #4000.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="54024886" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/4000" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/4000/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/4000">#4000</a> from adrian-wang/comment and squashes the following commits:

<a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/commit/9c24fc4e521b1eec86ebe9c55ec22a5a3dadcb8a/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/commit/9c24fc4e521b1eec86ebe9c55ec22a5a3dadcb8a"><tt>9c24fc4</tt></a> [Daoyuan Wang] some comments

Add extractor for SparseVector and DenseVector in MLlib to save some code while performing pattern matching on Vectors. For example, previously we may use:

     vec match {
          case dv: DenseVector =&gt;
            val values = dv.values
            ...
          case sv: SparseVector =&gt;
            val indices = sv.indices
            val values = sv.values
            val size = sv.size
            ...
      }

with extractor it is:

    vec match {
        case DenseVector(values) =&gt;
          ...
        case SparseVector(size, indices, values) =&gt;
          ...
    }

