This PR tries to fix the Hive tests failure encountered in PR <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="48081756" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/3157" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/3157/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/3157">#3157</a> by cleaning `lib_managed` before building assembly jar against Hive 0.13.1 in `dev/run-tests`. Otherwise two sets of datanucleus jars would be left in `lib_managed` and may mess up class paths while executing Hive test suites. Please refer to [this thread] [1] for details. A clean build would be even safer, but we only clean `lib_managed` here to save build time.

This PR also takes the chance to clean up some minor typos and formatting issues in the comments.

[1]: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="48081756" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/3157" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/3157/hovercard?comment_id=67656488&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/3157#issuecomment-67656488">#3157 (comment)</a>

