…le name

This PR enables the Web UI storage tab to show the in-memory table name instead of the mysterious query plan string as the name of the in-memory columnar RDD.

Note that after <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load issue title" data-id="43584969" data-permission-text="Issue title is private" data-url="https://github.com/apache/spark/issues/2501" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/apache/spark/pull/2501/hovercard" href="https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/2501">#2501</a>, a single columnar RDD can be shared by multiple in-memory tables, as long as their query results are the same. In this case, only the first cached table name is shown. For example:

```sql
CACHE TABLE first AS SELECT * FROM src;
CACHE TABLE second AS SELECT * FROM src;
```

The Web UI only shows "In-memory table first".

